It calls the cloud service behind the Remeha Home app (BDR Thermea:
https://api.bdrthermea.net and its login https://remehalogin.bdrthermea.net)
with the e-mail and the password of the user's Remeha Home account, the way
the app does. BDR Thermea publishes no documentation for it. Remeha, Baxi,
De Dietrich and Brötje are trademarks of the BDR Thermea Group; this
integration is not affiliated with nor endorsed by BDR Thermea.

Protocol knowledge
------------------
The login flow, the routes, the fields of the answers and their quirks (local
times written with a Z, the daily energy) come from the community integration
"Remeha Home" for Home Assistant and its documentation of the API:
  - remeha_home by msvisser (https://github.com/msvisser/remeha_home);
  - its maintained fork by hugo-leij
    (https://github.com/hugo-leij/remeha_home), documentation/api.md.
These projects carry no license file: only facts about the service were taken
from them (endpoints, field names, measured behaviour), never code. The answers
to wrong credentials, to a refused token and to a refused refresh token were
checked against the service itself. This integration is an independent
JavaScript implementation.
